# Waveshare ESP32-P4-NANO-WIFI6-DB (SKU 35554, and the KIT-A..D bundles)
#
# Build it with:
#   idf.py -B build.nanodb -D SDKCONFIG=build.nanodb/sdkconfig \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;boards/nano_wifi6_db_p4.defaults" build
#
# The NANO rebuilt around a dual-band radio: an ESP32-C5-MINI-1U instead of the
# C6, on an external antenna. Everything else is the family layout, and
# Waveshare publish the whole pin map on the board's documentation page, which
# is where all of this comes from:
#   Ethernet (IP101GRI): CRS_DV 28, RXD0 29, RXD1 30, MDC 31, TXD0 34, TXD1 35,
#                        TX_EN 49, REF_CLK 50 (input from the PHY), RESET 51,
#                        MDIO 52, PHY address 1 - the firmware defaults.
#   microSD: CLK 43, CMD 44, D0 39, D1 40, D2 41, D3 42, and SD_VDD_EN on 45,
#            "low to enable" in their own words, so active low as we default.
#   Capture I2C: SDA 7, SCL 8. That bus is busy here - the codec, the touch
#            controller, the backlight and the camera SCCB all sit on it - but
#            addresses do not collide with the bridge's.
#   BOOT button: GPIO 35, which is also Ethernet TXD1, the sharing the password
#            reset already handles.
#   Console: UART0 on 37/38, as on the NANO, whose Type-C reaches them through a
#            USB-to-UART bridge. CONFIRM on hardware: the DB's page says "power,
#            flashing and serial debugging" without naming the bridge, and a
#            console pointed at a port the board does not have looks exactly
#            like a device stuck at boot (#42).
#   Camera: "XCLK / RESET not connected", so there is no RESETN to drive.
#
# The CSI connector is the 15-pin, 1.0 mm Raspberry Pi one - measured off the
# board photograph against the 2.54 mm header next to it (1.09 mm pitch, ~15
# contacts), and consistent with the kit, which pairs an RPi Camera (B) with a
# plain 15-pin FFC cable. So a Geekworm C790 ribbon plugs straight in. The
# 15-to-22-pin cable in the kit is for a Pi 5 camera, not for this socket.
#
# Both 2x13 headers are drawn in board_header.c from Waveshare's own pinout
# picture. One thing on them is worth knowing here: the right-hand header brings
# out USBD_P and USBD_N, the P4's high-speed USB, so the target can be wired
# from the header instead of the Type-A socket.
#
# NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. Configured from the vendor's pin table and
# published so owners can try it. Waveshare has not put a schematic out for this
# SKU yet, so the console CONFIRM above is the one to check first.

# --- flash and partitions ---------------------------------------------------
# 16 MB Nor flash, 32 MB PSRAM in the chip's package.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_16mb.csv"

# --- silicon revision -------------------------------------------------------
# This one is not a choice. The board carries an ESP32-P4NRW32X - the marking is
# legible in Waveshare's own photograph - and the X part is the rev 3.x silicon:
# Espressif's "ESP32-P4 Chip Revision v3.x" guide names ESP32-P4NRW16X and
# ESP32-P4NRW32X as its products, and the older NRW32 is end of life.
#
# So this board gets the rev 3.x image and only that: a pre-3.0 build declares
# max chip rev 1.99 and the bootloader would refuse it. The same switch also
# compiles in the faster capture path, which is the consolation prize.
CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=n
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_300=y

# --- updates ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_UPDATE_URL="https://espkvm.github.io/espkvm/firmware/p4-nano-wifi6-db/manifest.json"

# --- WiFi co-processor ------------------------------------------------------
# An ESP32-C5, not the C6 every other board here uses, so the esp-hosted profile
# changes with it. The pins are the ones we already know - CLK 18, CMD 19,
# D0-D3 14/15/16/17, C5_CHIP_PU on 54 - which is exactly what esp-hosted's
# "ESP32-P4X-Function-EV-Board with on-board C5" preset declares, so that preset
# is the one to pick. (The plain Function-EV preset moves CLK and CMD to 33 and
# 4 when the co-processor is a C5, which is a different board's wiring.)
#
# The C5 is dual-band, so this is the first board here that can join a 5 GHz
# network. Untested: the co-processor's own firmware has to be an esp-hosted
# build that matches this component, and nobody has powered one up yet.
CONFIG_KVM_WIFI=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_P4X_C5_DEV_BOARD_FUNC_BOARD=y
CONFIG_SLAVE_IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_CP_TARGET_ESP32C5=y
# As everywhere else: esp-hosted must not bring the link up from its boot
# constructor, or it races the microSD for the one SD host controller.
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_AUTO_CALL_INIT_BEFORE_APP_MAIN=n

# --- microSD ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_SD_PWR_GPIO=45

# --- capture reset ----------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_TC358743_RST_GPIO=-1

# Which board this is: names it in the console and picks the expansion header
# the Pins tab draws.
CONFIG_KVM_BOARD_WAVESHARE_NANO_WIFI6_DB=y
